points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Showing Interest"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You show interest in people you meet by asking them common personal questions, often related to their work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">You can ask colleagues casual questions about:</span> <br /><li>their commute to work<br /><li>what part of the city they live in <br /><li>what they like for lunch<br /><li>their family life"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">You avoid asking colleagues personal questions about: </span> <li>their romantic life<br /><li>personal health conditions<br /><li>detailed family history"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How long does it take you to come to work?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When did you start working here?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How do you like your job?"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le18ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "almost there"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " almost finished a task or almost arrived at a place"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: <span class=\"strong\">Boss</span>: Did you complete that expense report? <span class=\"strong\">Employee</span>: I'm almost there, just a few more pages."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob10aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about work."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "portions"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "certain amounts of food to serve one person"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The sauce portions for each cheesecake must all taste the same."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob10aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "saucepan "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a round cooking pan  used for frying or making sauces "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The saucepan must be heated up before the cooking starts."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob10aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to catch on"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to become better at a new process of work"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Vanessa is really catching on with the daily routine at her chef job."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob10aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to show me the ropes "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to show a new person at work how something is done  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Daniel is showing Vanessa the ropes, so she's learning quickly."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob10aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "culinary "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " related to cooking, always followed by a noun "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Vanessa gained a lot of culinary skills from college."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob10aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to demonstrate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to show with action how something is done "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Vanessa demonstrates fine culinary skills in her cooking."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le18ob10aud06"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking Obligations (What I Have To Do)"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When describing our job responsibilities, we use have to  + infinitive to talk about an obligation or things that are necessary to do."}, {"type": "example", "content": " I have to put strawberries on the cake. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have to work everyday. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose your current job or imagine a job that you want to have in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 5 sentences describing what you have to do in this job. (e.g. <span class=\"italic\">I have to work weekends.</span>)"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read one sentence to your partner. He/she will try to guess what job you are describing. If they can't guess, read another one."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you are finished, listen to your partner and try to guess the job he/she is describing. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write sentences about a job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about what I have to do in my job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I listen to my partner's job description and try to guess the job."}]}], "type": "sena"}